;;; Converting a bignum to a float (FLOAT, COERCE, mixed-type arithmetic) takes the top 64 bits and looks
;;; at the bits below them only for a possible tie. Powers of two and their neighbours, values around
;;; 2^53 * 2^k with and without a sticky bit, negative numbers, random wide values: round to nearest even
;;; as before; the expected values are those of the build before the change, which agree with SBCL.

